 "notes": "Fig.1 (e-print plots/ma_fa.pdf, vector). Cosmological constraint on axion self-coupling parametrized by f_a in the (m_a, 1/f_a) plane; excluded region is ABOVE the plotted boundary (large 1/f_a = small f_a). Reported curve is the blue boundary (T_osc ~ sqrt(m_a M_pl)), which the paper presents as the strongest constraint, optimized over the oscillation temperature. Alternative weaker scenarios also shown: green (T_osc=1keV, most conservative) and red (T_osc=1keV, power-law growth). Grey regions are pre-existing BH superradiance limits, not this work. Bound derived from requiring decaying-DM fraction f_dDM<=2.62% at 2sigma (Eq.15-16). Assumes axion is all of dark matter with post-inflationary isocurvature power spectrum; independent of any SM coupling. Axis calibration from vector tick marks. y-axis units GeV^-1 (paper labels f_a^-1 [GeV^-1]).",
